  print("Current pattern:", _command_re)\n    print("Case-insensitive pattern:", _command_re_case_insensitive)\n    \n    # Test cases\n    test_lines = [\n        "READ SERR 3",\n        "read serr 3", \n        "READ TERR 1",\n        "read terr 1",\n        "READ serr 3",\n        "read SERR 3"\n    ]\n    \n    # Compile with current pattern\n    current_pattern = re.compile(_command_re)\n    \n    # Compile with case-insensitive flag\n    case_insensitive_pattern = re.compile(_command_re_with_flag, re.IGNORECASE)\n    \n    print("\\n=== Testing current pattern ===")\n    for line in test_lines:\n        match = current_pattern.match(line)\n        if match:\n            print(f"\'{line}\' -> MATCH")\n        else:\n            print(f"\'{line}\' -> NO MATCH")\n            \n    print("\\n=== Testing case-insensitive pattern ===")\n    for line in test_lines:\n        match = case_insensitive_pattern.match(line)\n        if match:\n            print(f"\'{line}\' -> MATCH")\n        else:\n            print(f"\'{line}\' -> NO MATCH")\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    test_command_matching()\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\nOBSERVATION:\n\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\rFile created successfully at: /testbed/simple_test.py\n\r\r\n</tool_response>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<tool_call>\n<function=bash>\n<parameter=command>\ncd /testbed && python simple_test.py\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\nOBSERVATION:\n\rCurrent pattern: READ [TS]ERR(\\s+[0-9]+)+\nCase-insensitive pattern: (READ|read) ([TS]|ts)ERR(\\s+[0-9]+)+\n\n=== Testing current pattern ===\n\'READ SERR 3\' -> MATCH\n\'read serr 3\' -> NO MATCH\n\'READ TERR 1\' -> MATCH\n\'read terr 1\' -> NO MATCH\n\'READ serr 3\' -> NO MATCH\n\'read SERR 3\' -> NO MATCH\n\n=== Testing case-insensitive pattern ===\n\'READ SERR 3\' -> MATCH\n\'read serr 3\' -> MATCH\n\'READ TERR 1\' -> MATCH\n\'read terr 1\' -> MATCH\n\'READ serr 3\' -> MATCH\n\'read SERR 3\' -> MATCH\n\r\r\n</tool_response>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nPerfect! This confirms the issue. The current regex pattern only matches uppercase commands, but we want it to match both uppercase and lowercase commands.\n\n## Phase 3: Fix Analysis\n\nBased on my exploration, here\'s what I found:\n\n1. **Problem**: In `/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/qdp.py`, line 63, the regex pattern `_command_re = r"READ [TS]ERR(\\s+[0-9]+)+"` only matches uppercase commands like "READ SERR 3" but not lowercase commands like "read serr 3".\n\n2. **Location**: The issue is in the `_line_type` function in the qdp.py file.\n\n3. **Root Cause**: The regex pattern uses literal uppercase characters, making it case-sensitive.\n\n4. **Solution**: We need to make the command matching case-insensitive. The simplest approach is to add the `re.IGNORECASE` flag to the regex compilation.\n\n5. **Minimal Change**: We can modify the regex compilation to use the `re.IGNORECASE` flag, which will make the entire pattern case-insensitive without changing the pattern itself.\n\n## Phase 4: Fix Implementation\n\nLet me implement the fix:\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=str_replace_editor>\n<parameter=command>\nstr_replace\n</parameter>\n<parameter=path>\n/testbed/astropy/io/ascii/qdp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_str>\n    _type_re = rf"^\\s*((?P<command>{_command_re})|(?P<new>{_new_re})|(?P<data>{_data_re})?\\s*(\\!(?P<comment>.*))?\\s*$"\n    _line_type_re = re.compile(_type_re)\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_str>\n    _type_re = rf"^\\s*((?P<command>{_command_re})|(?P<new>{_new_re})|(?P<data>{_data_re})?\\s*(\\!(?P<comment>.*))?\\s*$"\n    _line_type_re = re.compile(_type_re, re.IGNORECASE)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\nOBSERVATION:\n\r\r\rThe file /testbed/astropy/io/ascii/qdp.py has been edited. Here\'s the result of r